TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2) - T3 2020 Assignment","overview":"Design a space mission benefiting Australia and identify main elements of its space segment, demonstrating understanding of launch, orbits and space systems via preliminary mission plan using software (STK, PIGI, or other) supplemented by hand calculations."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all required info (primary mission, need, number of spacecraft and why, users/operators/customers) to high standard with detailed descriptions and appropriate literature references."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions lack specific details and/or referencing is incomplete."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements not addressed. Poor descriptions and lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high-level understanding of design procedure, clearly addresses mission and course concepts. All major requirements (launch site/vehicle and rationale, orbit type/characteristics/elements, maneuvers, ground facilities, communication frequency, mission duration and EOL plan) well supported with quality evidence (screenshots, software files, hand calculations, literature). Comprehensive, accurate, persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding but design may be inconsistent, unclear, or contain errors. Major requirements addressed but lacking detail or evidence. Content not fully comprehensive or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding. Major requirements not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content incomplete and not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions drawn from report evidence."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions reached but generic or lacking specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Clear logical engineering report structure, easy to read, good writing/spelling/grammar/style, consistent formatting, concise executive summary/abstract, appropriate clear consistent figures/tables, references in text match list and properly cited."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Not professional level but uses headings/subheadings. Readable but flawed writing/spelling/grammar/style. Figures/tables labelled but formatting unclear/inconsistent affecting context. References mostly correct and match list."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Poorly structured, incoherent, lacks understanding of section purpose. Difficult to read, poor writing with many spelling/grammar errors and inappropriate style. Presentation impedes reading due to inconsistent formatting and unlabelled figures/tables. References not cited or inconsistent."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Launch"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R7","met":"partial","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R8","met":"yes","where":"Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R10","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Orbit","issue":"RAAN value 27.33° linked to launch facility latitude, incorrect definition; Argument of Latitude used to replace AOP/ν but not valid classic element set; e=0 claim circular but J2 perturbed SSO typically slightly eccentric; no communication frequency band defined despite requirement."},{"where":"Launch","issue":"Selects Vega E (first flight 2024 planned, not yet proven in 2020 assignment) without performance verification or mass budget; equatorial launch benefit argument applied to SSO retrograde which reduces benefit; references Wikipedia timeline as primary source despite ban."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Access report shows mean ~580s contact but fails to compute daily communication opportunities/revisit to GBR; no link budget, frequency, or data rate."}],"overall":"Solid mission concept with good rationale for Australia, single-sat SSO justified, STK evidence included. Minor technical inaccuracies and missing comms details keep it at adequate rather than accomplished overall.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Primary mission (coral reef monitoring benefiting Australia), single spacecraft rationale (bleaching over days/weeks), users/operators clearly stated with context, supported by references. Meets all required info to high standard.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"coral reef and ocean monitoring. The satellite must provide images for a fluid lensing tool"},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"only one satellite is required. This also just allows for simplicity"},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"likely be used by governmental and science agencies (e.g. CSIRO, BOM)"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":36.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"Demonstrates adequate understanding: launch vehicle/site with rationale, SSO orbit type, 600km altitude, inclination calculation and table of elements, maneuver note, ground station with STK access report, EOL drag sail. Some errors: RAAN described as launch facility location, Arg of lat misuse, swath not quantified, comm frequency band missing, Vega E not yet flown but used as definitive choice. Evidence present (Image 1-5, plots, tables).","evidence":[{"where":"Launch","quote":"proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle – launched from the Guiana Space Centre"},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"altitude of 600km requires a mean inclination of 97.7924° for the satellite to remain sun-synchronous"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"Satellite-ZYZZsat-To-Facility-Mt_Pleasant_Radio_Observatory: Access Summary Report"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":5.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusion summarizes mission segments and reiterates launch, orbit, ground station and benefit but lacks quantitative conclusions drawn from STK results (e.g., coverage performance, contact duration stats) and risk/mitigation. Generic but appropriate.","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"fully described satellite configuration has been constructed. The initial problem of not catching coral bleaching events"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":10.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Has logical structure, headings, figures labelled partially, readable but formatting inconsistent (tables broken, STK screenshots lacking titles), uses Wikipedia despite prohibition, references not properly formatted, executive summary present but not concise. Meets adequate level.","evidence":[{"where":"Image 4","quote":""},{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."}]}]}
